Patch — sglang/gravityocr_selfspec.patch
  Copyright 2026 Trillion Labs. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
  A diff against the base commit above. It modifies 22 upstream source files
  under python/sglang/srt/ and python/pyproject.toml, where it relaxes the
  torchao and torchcodec pins (sglang/overrides.txt records the versions used).
  The changes register the SELFSPEC_DIFFUSION speculative-decoding algorithm
  (block-diffusion draft, autoregressive verify) for GLM-OCR checkpoints, add
  the scheduler, cache and CUDA-graph support it needs, and add optional runtime
  optimizations. They also change four upstream behaviours for every server
  built from the patch: the server-info endpoints, the logged server arguments
  and the request dumps no longer contain the API and admin keys; every
  tokenizer worker checks the keys; the shared-memory segment that hands
  the server arguments to the tokenizer workers is created private and is
  never read when another user owns it; and a single-node server's
  torch.distributed rendezvous runs on 127.0.0.1 with a store that listens
  on loopback only. The modified files keep their upstream copyright headers.
  Pure code; no model weights.
